WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.440
Speaker 1: I want to talk about 2024 and 2024
as possible Republican contenders.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.060
I'm not talking about Donald Trump here.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.139
Donald Trump is running, at least for now,
unless he drops out.

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:14.530
I'm talking about the other possible contenders
in Fox Business.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:18.529
And actually Fox News in general has regularly
been putting up images like the one we're

00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:19.730
putting up now.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.580
This one is called possible Republican candidates
in 2024.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.140
And indeed, Donald Trump isn't on that list
because Trump is not a possible candidate.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.750
He is a candidate.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.290
The folks listed include former Vice President
Mike Pence, current Florida Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.000
Virginia Governor Glenn Youngkin.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Larry Hogan.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.060
Asa Hutchinson.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:42.230
Senator Tim Scott, Mike Pompeo, Nikki Haley
and Chris Christie.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:48.239
And what's really interesting about this list
is that it's a really scary list.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:53.320
And I thought, let's just talk a little bit
about the people that are sort of considered

00:00:53.320 --> 00:01:00.220
contenders to be Republican presidential nominee,
at least hypothetically, and think through

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.809
how extreme the party has gotten.

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:08.500
At the end of the segment, I'll tell you who
would be my choice if I wanted to to to limit

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
damage to the country.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.550
And I'll tell you in a moment, you've got
Mike Pence.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:20.200
Mike Pence, wildly against abortion, skeptical
about climate change, has a history of opposing

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:27.290
LGBT rights, wants to build that wall with
Mexico, has been against Obamacare, never

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:31.829
mind stronger health care programs than Obamacare.

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:38.689
Seems very interested in religion more and
more officially playing a role in civil government

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:45.469
and also just on a personal level is kind
of a kind of a moron in the sense that even

00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:52.400
though Trump's supporters were calling for
him to be hanged, he still doesn't totally

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.040
denounce Trump, although he kind of has.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.729
And he said, I think we'll have better candidates
or whatever.

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:05.070
It's just a guy who is both spineless and
has some of the worse political views.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.939
That's one alternative to Trump for the Republican
Party.

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:09.450
Okay, it's pretty bad.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.700
Then you've got Ron DeSantis.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:16.520
Ron DeSantis, whose record as Florida governor
is one of regularly signing into law bills

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:23.610
that restrict abortion in Florida, loves restricting
abortion, regularly weakens gun laws in Florida

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:30.879
at every opportunity supported repealing the
Affordable Care Act, has a horrible environmental

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:37.640
record in Florida, loves fossil fuels, opportunities
to use more fossil fuels and make it easier

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.070
to use fossil fuels.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:47.700
DeSantis loves it, and in addition to that,
DeSantis is arguably more competent than Trump

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.480
and as a result, could be extraordinarily
more dangerous if he became the president

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.430
of the United States.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:03:01.530
Then you've got arguably one of the slightly
less extreme people on the list, Larry Hogan.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:06.640
But you look at his record and it's horrifying
against abortion, as most of these people

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:12.141
are against the Affordable Care Act tried
to repeal the Affordable Care Act, supports

00:03:12.141 --> 00:03:15.769
the oil and gas industry backwards, just totally
backwards.

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:20.330
And we're supposed to see him as less extreme
to pick a senator.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.730
Tim Scott from South Carolina.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:29.220
Tim Scott against abortion, wants to restrict
access to abortion, is against any gun safety

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.500
regulations.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.660
Supports every tax cut that's proposed.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.020
Skeptical about climate science, even though
he doesn't actually know anything about it.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.879
So I could go on and on and on.

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:40.769
It's an insane list of people.

00:03:40.769 --> 00:03:46.390
Now, if I look at the list and you said to
me, David, and this is something that probably

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.790
would bring tears to your eyes if you came
to and said, David, it's going to be one of

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.210
the people on this list.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:57.519
Tears, if you knew it was going to be one
of these people who defeat the Democrat.

00:03:57.519 --> 00:03:58.980
Who would you choose?

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.360
The to me, it seems clear that it's Chris
Christie.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.159
And I'm glad to hear from other people and
see your opinions.

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:11.209
But when I look at this list, Pence, DeSantis,
Youngkin, Hogan Hutchinson, Scott Pompeo,

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:16.010
Haley, Christie and then Trump, who has already
declared to me, it's Chris Christie.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:23.650
Chris Christie is a smart guy in a way that
a lot of these other people aren't.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:29.080
Maybe DeSantis, but but you know, like Pence
and Yang.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:37.570
Christie is a smart guy, former prosecutor,
more moderate socially to some degree because

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:40.620
of his experience as governor.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:47.310
And a Northeastern governor understands compromise
and working across the aisle in a way that

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.360
some of these other people do.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.710
Now, I know people will write to me and say,
David Christie's insane.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:52.880
What are you talking about?

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:53.880
Remember?

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:57.670
It's if one of these people was going to be
the next president.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.450
I think I'm choosing Chris Christie.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.130
And I'm interested to hear from others.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:06.300
But it's shaping up to be a pretty scary list.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.340
Now, fortunately or unfortunately, I don't
know.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:12.650
You know, names like Don Junior are sometimes
thrown around.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.810
They're not showing up on this list, at least
not yet.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:06:37.209
And I think we should probably be happy about
that.

